      "problem": "What is the projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+{z}^{2}=1$ and the plane $z=1$ onto the $xy$-plane?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z=1$, we substitute $z=1$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+{1}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(x-2)^{2} \\\\ y & =\\pm 2(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two intersecting lines: $y=2(x-2)$ and $y=-2(x-2).$",
